  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `camcraft_post::machine` has a new pure data type, `MachineTree`, and a new reader, `parse_mch_tree` (new file `crates/post/src/machine/tree.rs`).\n- The reader keeps each part of `kinematics.default.parts`: its `id`, `name`, `type`, the index of its parent, and the facts that the file states (`travel`, `axis`, `pivot`, `offset`, `direction`, the spindle body, the tool station).\n- All lengths are in mm. The reader uses the unit factor of `parse_mch`. An angle is not scaled.\n- Each linear and rotary part has a moving side. An axis that is an ancestor of a `head` part moves the tool. Each other axis moves the table. A tree with no head states no side.\n- A malformed tree refuses. The message names the part id and the key.\n- `Machine`, `parse_mch` and the existing checks do not change.\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` has a short note about the new reader.\n\n## Cause\n\n`collect_axes` in `parse.rs` flattens the part tree into `Machine.axes`. The parent chain is lost. A machine model (#2574) needs the chain.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew suite `crates/post/tests/machine_tree.rs` (8 tests):\n\n- `every_shipped_machine_file_reads_as_a_tree`: each of the 45 `assets/machines/*.mch` files parses. The tree and `parse_mch` state the same number of axes.\n- `the_three_axis_vmc_keeps_its_parent_chain` (`vmc.mch`)\n- `the_tilt_head_puts_the_head_chain_on_the_tool_side` (`tilthead.mch`)\n- `an_inch_file_scales_lengths_and_keeps_angles` (`tormach-770mx-microarc4.mch`)\n- `a_hand_written_inch_tree_scales_each_length_and_no_angle`\n- `the_mirror_form_default_machine_states_no_part_tree` (`3axis-vmc.mch`)\n- `a_tree_with_no_head_states_no_moving_side`\n- `a_malformed_tree_refuses_by_part_id_and_key` (17 malformed trees)\n\nMutation results:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `mod.rs` as on `upstream/main` (no `tree` module) | red: the suite does not compile (`unresolved imports ... parse_mch_tree`) |\n| No unit factor on `travel` | red: 2 tests fail |\n| Moving side swapped | red: 4 tests fail |\n| Duplicate `id` guard off | red: `a_malformed_tree_refuses_by_part_id_and_key` |\n| Unknown `type` accepted | red: `a_malformed_tree_refuses_by_part_id_and_key` |\n| Fix restored | green: 8 passed |\n\nThe suite was written before the reader. Its first run on unchanged code did not finish (the build was stopped at a time limit). The first mutation above is the proof that it is red without the change.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (71 steps, 0 failed, on base `3e615d653`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No code uses `MachineTree` yet. The simulator work of #2574 is the first user.\n- `3axis-vmc.mch` is written in the mirror form (`kinematics.static`). It states no part tree, so it reads as an empty tree. The 3-axis parent chain is pinned on `vmc.mch`.\n- Most shipped 3-axis files put the `head` beside the axis chain (`base > col > ram > sld` and `base > head`). By the rule of the issue, all their axes read as table side. Only `tilthead.mch`, `sinker-edm.mch` and `millturn.mch` state a tool-side axis. A correct model needs those machine files nested as the machine moves. This PR does not change a machine file. See `docs/decisions/2583-machine-tree.md`.\n- The tree door also refuses `zero_offset`, `rollover` and `sign_convention` on a part that is not a rotary, because it uses `trunnion::parse_axis_fields`. No shipped file states them there.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2554 touches `crates/post/src/machine/mod.rs` and `parse.rs`: the same files, different lines and functions. This PR adds two module lines in `mod.rs` and makes `rate`, `mm_factor` and `scale` `pub(super)` in `parse.rs`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nThe type is `feat`: the issue is an enhancement (`P4`), so this PR merges at the next cut.\n\nChangelog: Post: the `.mch` part tree is kept as `MachineTree` (`parse_mch_tree`), with the parent chain and the moving side of each axis, for the machine model (#2583).\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2583\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
